      "marks": 6,
      "answer": "$5x-10y-z=-25$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Primary method: obtain a vector parallel to the plane, e.g. $\\overrightarrow{CB}=2\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j$ [B1]; use scalar products to obtain an equation in $a,b,c$ [M1], e.g. $2a+b=0$, $a+5c=0$, or $a+b-5c=0$; obtain two correct equations [A1]; solve for a ratio [M1]; obtain $a:b:c=5:-10:-1$, or equivalent [A1]; and obtain $5x-10y-z=-25$, or equivalent [A1]. Alternative 1: obtain another plane vector, e.g. $\\overrightarrow{CD}=\\mathbf i+5\\mathbf k$ [B1]; obtain a second plane vector and form their vector product, e.g. $(2\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j)\\times(\\mathbf i+5\\mathbf k)$ [M1]; obtain two correct components [A1]; obtain $5\\mathbf i-10\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k$ [A1]; substitute to find $d$ [M1]; obtain the plane equation [A1]. Alternative 2: obtain a plane vector, e.g. $\\overrightarrow{DB}=\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j-5\\mathbf k$ [B1]; obtain a second and form a correct two-parameter plane equation [M1]; state e.g. $\\mathbf r=3\\mathbf i+4\\mathbf j+\\lambda(\\mathbf i+5\\mathbf k)+\\mu(\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j-5\\mathbf k)$ [A1]; state three equations in $x,y,z,\\lambda,\\mu$ [A1]; eliminate $\\lambda,\\mu$ [M1]; obtain the plane equation [A1]. Alternative 3: substitute $B,C$ to obtain $3a+4b=d$ and $a+3b=d$ [B1]; substitute $D$ and eliminate one unknown entirely [M1]; obtain two correct equations in two unknowns [A1]; solve for their ratio [M1]; obtain $a:b:c=5:-10:-1$ or $a:c:d=5:-1:-25$ or $b:c:d=10:1:25$ [A1]; obtain the plane equation [A1]. Alternative 4: substitute $B,C$ for $3a+4b=d$ and $a+3b=d$ [B1]; solve to obtain $a:b:d$ [M2]; obtain $a:b:d=1:-2:-5$ [A1]; substitute $C$ to obtain $c$ [M1]; obtain the plane equation [A1]. Total 6.",
